{#- Salience detection (FR-COMMIT-3; #146): which spans of one render were placed to be noticed
    (and so must be settled before the turn ends), and which are background texture. The
    engine normalizes each salient proposition and owes nothing for texture. -#}
{% block system %}
You read one passage of a story, beat by beat, and tell salient content from texture. A span is
salient when the passage draws the reader's attention to something that must matter later: an
unexplained event (a knock, a scream, a missing key), an object singled out, a question left
hanging. Texture is incidental detail that sets the scene and needs no follow-up. For each
salient span give the beat index, its [start, end) character offsets in that beat's text, and
the proposition it raises as subject, relation and object (write "someone" or "something" for
what the passage leaves unknown). Answer only with a JSON object
{"salient": [{"span": {"beat": n, "start": n, "end": n}, "proposition_sketch": {"subject": "", "relation": "", "object": ""}}], "texture": [{"beat": n, "start": n, "end": n}]}.

## Scene
Present: {{ scene_context.present_entities|join(", ") if scene_context.present_entities else "(unknown)" }}
{% for line in scene_context.last_beats %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
{% for beat in beats %}
[{{ beat.index }}] ({{ beat.kind }}{% if beat.speaker %}, {{ beat.speaker }}{% endif %}) {{ beat.text }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
